{"meta":{"id":"dm.aHR0cDovL3NlcnZlcjEuZGhha2Ftb3ZpZS5jb20vTW92aWVzL0hvbGx5d29vZC8xOTk5LS1CZWZvcmUvVGhlJTIwTmF2aWdhdG9yJTIwQSUyME1lZGlldmFsJTIwT2R5c3NleSUyMCUyODE5ODglMjkv","type":"movie","name":"The Navigator A Medieval Odyssey","poster":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w342/3jgWf292UUNZyaaLppFlYWFpDOE.jpg","background":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w780/a5kImJOOgKOiCNHvYwTJPnJMzQr.jpg","description":"Cumberland, 1348. The plague is spreading in medieval England. The remote village of little Griffin is also threatened. But the 9-year-old boy has a recurring dream that holds the key to a tiny hope of survival: a lake with a coffin floating on it. A white church with an iron cross. A falling glove. A falling silhouette. A torch tumble through a dark shaft into infinity. With his brother he recognizes in it a prophecy to escape the Black Death. So they embark with a few men on a journey to a distant cathedral, where they want to set up an iron cross as an offering to God. Her path leads them through a deep and dark mine shaft into an unknown land and completely outlandish time - into the present-day New Zealand of the 1980s.\n\nReleased 15 Dec 1988 · Australia, New Zealand · Language: English · 92 min\nStudio: Arenafilm, Film Investment Corporation of New Zealand, The Australian Film Commission\n\nOn your server — Audio: English","releaseInfo":"1988","genres":["Adventure","Fantasy","Mystery","Hollywood"],"imdbRating":"6.2","imdb_id":"tt0095709","moviedb_id":34637,"tmdbId":34637,"runtime":"92 min","cast":["Bruce Lyons","Chris Haywood","Hamish McFarlane","Marshall Napier","Noel Appleby","Paul Livingston","Sarah Peirse","Mark Wheatley"],"director":["Vincent Ward"],"writer":["Geoff Chapple","Kely Lyons","Vincent Ward"],"released":"1988-12-15T00:00:00.000Z","slogan":"An Odyssey Across Time.","country":"Australia, New Zealand","language":"English","app_extras":{"cast":[{"name":"Vincent Ward","character":"Director","photo":"https://image.tmdb.org/t/p/w185/wB7WbhfrcJQl1nc0AbCjJ26d1eE